dence for T-cell cross-reactivity and LPS structure [P0146][P0573]. NSCLC shows independent lung microbiome effects [P0352]. GI tumors depend on etiology [P0113]. RCC sensitive to antibiotics [P0090]. Prostate shows reverse correlation for Akkermansia [P0270]. TNBC shows chemo vs ICI difference [P0057]. Intratumoral bacteria also play a role [P0535][P0457].\n\n**Paragraph 2:**\nDistinguish evidence. Mouse models allow causal inference (FMT, KO) [P0146][P0573]. Human data is largely observational (cohorts, sequencing) [P0535]. Extrapolation risk [P0146].\n\n**Table:**\nFill rows based on `table_tasks` and source content.\n\n**JSON Structure:**\n`{\"body_markdown\": \"...\", \"issues\": []}`\n\n**Self-Correction on Citation Reuse:**\nThe instruction says \"同一篇可以跨段使用，但用途必须不同\" (Same paper can be used across paragraphs, but usage must be different).\nP0535, P0146, P0573 are in P01 and P02.\nIn P01: Used for tumor type examples.\nIn P02: Used for model system evidence levels.\nThis is acceptable.\nP0080, P0388, P0269, P0438 are *only* in Table tasks. I will cite them in the table cells.\nP0057, P0090, P0113, P0270, P0352, P0457 are in P01 and Table. I will cite them in P01 text, and can cite them again in the table if needed for specific data points, but to avoid clutter, I might rely on the text for the general claim and table for the specific comparison. However, the Table Task says \"Source\" column. I must put the citation in the table cell. So `[P0090]` will appear in P01 text and Table Row 3. This is allowed as long as the *content* isn't mechanically repeated (Text: narrative; Table: structured comparison).\n\nLet's write."
